      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:839",
      "id": "done_when-1",
      "reason": "a worker reading \"for the session as live or queued\" will most naturally call `crew view live --session <s>` (the same shape the obligations view requires), which returns every run in the project, and its equality assertion then either fails spuriously or gets \"fixed\" by widening the pane's population to runs the session does not own.",
      "text": "the deliverable's reference is \"the runs `reckon crew view live` lists for the session as live or queued\", but `serve_crew_view`'s live branch (reckon/mcp_views.py:4770-4813) narrows to a session only when `mine` is true (a bare `session` argument just marks ownership and never filters rows), and applies no phase filter unless a single `--phase` value is given \u2014 so the default read returns every live pointer phase for the whole project, including `awaiting-upstream`, `held`, `blocked-upstream` and `launch-failed` (reckon/crew/runs.py:2420), not the \"live or queued\" set the sentence names",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:839",
      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "the reference needs the same rule s122 already applies to duties (run-scoped, naming the run's own id) stated in the section, or the implementation unions a phantom empty run id and the pane's \"empty means nothing is owned\" guarantee breaks in production while the gate stays green.",
      "text": "\"The two sets must be equal\" does not hold against the obligations view as it stands: that view's duties include project-scoped rows with no run, `_index_lag_notice` (reckon/crew/obligations.py:2920-2926, documented \"not run-scoped: it belongs to the project, so every session working it sees the same row\", emitted into every session's payload), which carries no run id \u2014 and the four-run temporary fixture drives neither that notice nor any other run-less duty, so the assertion passes while a real store's union contains a duty that names no run",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    }
  ],
